<!-- ── CLI Commands ── -->
<section class="sec" id="cli-commands">
  <div class="sec-title">🔧 CLI Commands — agent-eval</div>
  <div class="sec-sub">All commands installed with the base SDK. Run <code>agent-eval &lt;command&gt; --help</code> for the full flag reference at any time.</div>

  <div class="cls-card" id="cli-init">
    <div class="cls-head"><span class="cls-name">agent-eval init</span><span class="kind fn">CLI</span><span class="cls-src">cli/main.py</span></div>
    <div class="cls-body">
      <div class="cls-desc">Interactive wizard — prompts for <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code>/<code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code> and saves them to a <code>.env</code> file (project-local, global <code>~/.agent-evaluator/.env</code>, or print export commands). Takes no arguments.</div>
<pre>agent-eval init</pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cls-card" id="cli-check" style="margin-top:12px">
    <div class="cls-head"><span class="cls-name">agent-eval check</span><span class="kind fn">CLI</span><span class="cls-src">cli/main.py</span></div>
    <div class="cls-body">
      <div class="cls-desc">Shows API key status (masked), other <code>AGENT_EVALUATOR_*</code>/<code>OPENAI_*</code>/<code>ANTHROPIC_*</code>/<code>LANGCHAIN_*</code> settings, installed optional package status, and the loaded <code>.env</code> file path. Takes no arguments.</div>
<pre>agent-eval check</pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cls-card" id="cli-dashboard" style="margin-top:12px">
    <div class="cls-head"><span class="cls-name">agent-eval dashboard</span><span class="kind fn">CLI</span><span class="cls-src">cli/main.py</span></div>
    <div class="cls-body">
      <div class="cls-desc">Starts the FastAPI dashboard. Positional <code>results_dir</code> (default <code>./results</code>).</div>
      <table class="mtable"><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--host / --port</span></td><td>Bind host/port (default <code>127.0.0.1</code> / <code>8765</code>)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--open / --no-open</span></td><td>Auto-open browser after start (default: open)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--watch</span></td><td>Watch result files for changes and auto-refresh</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--offline</span></td><td>Cache CDN assets locally for offline use</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--title TITLE</span></td><td>Dashboard title (default: <code>'Agent Evaluator — Dev Dashboard'</code>)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--auth-token TOKEN</span></td><td>Require a Bearer token (or <code>AGENT_EVALUATOR_DASHBOARD_TOKEN</code> env var) to access the dashboard. Default: no auth (localhost-only assumption)</td></tr>
      </tbody></table>
<pre>agent-eval dashboard results/ --port 8080 --watch</pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cls-card" id="cli-diagnose" style="margin-top:12px">
    <div class="cls-head"><span class="cls-name">agent-eval diagnose</span><span class="kind fn">CLI</span><span class="cls-src">cli/diagnose.py</span></div>
    <div class="cls-body">
      <div class="cls-desc">Gate root-cause diagnosis (RCA) — the 3-stage detect → attribute → cross-reference procedure. Not a CI gate: informational only, exit code is always <code>0</code> once the file is read (<code>1</code> only if it can't be). Positional <code>result_file</code>.</div>
      <table class="mtable"><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--baseline PATH</span></td><td>Enables regression-based detection. Without it, falls back to detecting Gates whose current status is fail/warn</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--regression-threshold PCT</span></td><td>Allowed regression vs baseline (%), same definition as <code>gate --fail-on-regression</code> (default: 10)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--violation-db PATH</span></td><td>SQLite DB (<code>storage_backend="sqlite"</code>) for stage-3 cross-reference via <code>search_violations()</code>. Skipped if omitted/missing</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--json</span></td><td>Print the raw diagnosis result as JSON instead of the formatted report</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--show-diff</span></td><td>With <code>--baseline</code>: also resolve the actual git commit range between both reports' <code>lineage.git_commit</code> (plain <code>git diff --stat</code>/<code>git log</code>, no <code>gh</code> CLI). Silently omitted if unavailable</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--repo-path PATH</span></td><td>Git repository path for <code>--show-diff</code> (default: current directory)</td></tr>
      </tbody></table>
<pre>agent-eval diagnose results/ci_run.json --baseline results/baseline.json --show-diff</pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cls-card" id="cli-abtest" style="margin-top:12px">
    <div class="cls-head"><span class="cls-name">agent-eval abtest</span><span class="kind fn">CLI</span><span class="cls-src">cli/abtest.py</span></div>
    <div class="cls-body">
      <div class="cls-desc">Statistical A/B comparison of 2+ result JSON files. Not a CI gate — reports significance/effect size/sample-size warnings only, never pass/fail. 2 files → Welch's t-test (or mSPRT with <code>--sequential</code>); 3+ files → N-way pairwise with Benjamini-Hochberg FDR correction.</div>
      <table class="mtable"><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--metric NAME</span></td><td>TaskResult attribute or <code>task.extra</code> key to compare (default: <code>accuracy_score</code>)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--guardrail METRIC:DIRECTION:MAX_REGRESSION</span></td><td>Guardrail Metric (OEC), repeatable. <code>DIRECTION</code> is <code>higher_is_better</code>|<code>lower_is_better</code>. 2-file mode only, not with <code>--sequential</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--sequential</span></td><td>Use mSPRT always-valid inference instead of a fixed-sample t-test (safe to check results as they come in). Requires <code>--tau</code>, 2-file mode only</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--tau FLOAT</span></td><td>Mixture prior scale for <code>--sequential</code> — no implicit default, must be set explicitly</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--alpha FLOAT</span></td><td>Significance level for <code>--sequential</code> (default: 0.05)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--fdr-alpha FLOAT</span></td><td>Significance level after FDR correction, for 3+ files (default: 0.05)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--min-samples N</span></td><td>Sample count below which a sample-size warning is shown (default: 30)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--json</span></td><td>Print the raw comparison result as JSON instead of the formatted report</td></tr>
      </tbody></table>
<pre>agent-eval abtest results/v1.json results/v2.json --sequential --tau 0.05
agent-eval abtest results/v1.json results/v2.json results/v3.json  <span class="cm"># N-way + FDR</span></pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cls-card" id="cli-claims" style="margin-top:12px">
    <div class="cls-head"><span class="cls-name">agent-eval claims</span><span class="kind fn">CLI</span><span class="cls-src">cli/claims.py</span></div>
    <div class="cls-body">
      <div class="cls-desc">Terminal-friendly wrapper around <code>.aoo/claims.jsonl</code> team-scope claim management (<code>append_claim()</code>/<code>load_active_claims()</code>/<code>audit_claims()</code>) — used by <code>TeamConcurrencyConfig</code>/<code>LiveGuardrail</code> to detect overlapping work between concurrent developers.</div>
      <table class="mtable"><thead><tr><th>Subcommand</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td><span class="p">add PATH... --developer NAME</span></td><td>Open a new claim over one or more paths. <code>--developer auto</code> (or omitted) resolves via <code>git config user.name</code>. <code>--claim-id ID</code> to set explicitly (default: auto-generated <code>c-&lt;8 hex&gt;</code>)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">list</span></td><td>List currently active claims</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">release CLAIM_ID</span></td><td>Release an active claim by ID. <code>--force</code> records the release event even if the ID isn't currently active</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">audit --ttl-hours N</span></td><td>CI-friendly — exit <code>1</code> if any active claim exceeds the TTL (default 8.0h) or overlaps another claim's scope</td></tr>
      </tbody></table>
      <div class="cls-desc" style="margin-top:6px">All subcommands accept <code>--claims-path PATH</code> (default: <code>.aoo/claims.jsonl</code>).</div>
<pre>agent-eval claims add src/ --developer alex
agent-eval claims audit --ttl-hours 8</pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cls-card" id="cli-dataset" style="margin-top:12px">
    <div class="cls-head"><span class="cls-name">agent-eval dataset</span><span class="kind fn">CLI</span><span class="cls-src">cli/dataset.py</span></div>
    <div class="cls-body">
      <div class="cls-desc">Golden dataset lifecycle. For Phoenix dataset upload, use <code>agent-eval monitor --sync-datasets</code> instead.</div>
      <table class="mtable"><thead><tr><th>Subcommand</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td><span class="p">build</span></td><td>Auto-extract golden candidates from result JSON files. <code>--source DIR</code> · <code>--output DIR</code> · <code>--strategy failure_cases edge_cases high_value coverage_gap</code> (default: failure_cases + edge_cases) · <code>--max-cases N</code> (default 50) · <code>--no-review</code> · <code>--name FILE</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">promote result.json</span></td><td>Turn the tasks in the result's <code>insights.review_queue</code> (HITL queue) into golden regression cases. <code>--min-priority high</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">health golden.json --against v3.json</span></td><td>Golden-set coverage vs. current failure modes + stale / duplicate cases. <code>uncovered_failure_modes</code> = blind spots</td></tr>
      </tbody></table>
<pre>agent-eval dataset build --source results/ --strategy failure_cases high_value --max-cases 30
agent-eval dataset health golden.json --against v3.json</pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cls-card" id="cli-monitor" style="margin-top:12px">
    <div class="cls-head"><span class="cls-name">agent-eval monitor</span><span class="kind fn">CLI</span><span class="cls-src">cli/monitor.py</span></div>
    <div class="cls-body">
      <div class="cls-desc">Starts an Arize Phoenix server + OTLP span receiver for real-time tracing/error detection. Requires <code>pip install "agent-evaluator[otel]"</code>. Phoenix 13.x shares the UI + OTLP HTTP port (default 6006).</div>
      <table class="mtable"><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--port / --host</span></td><td>Phoenix UI + OTLP HTTP port/host (default: <code>6006</code> / <code>localhost</code>)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--no-open</span></td><td>Disable automatic browser launch</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--attach URL</span></td><td>Connect to an already-running Phoenix server instead of starting one</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--check</span></td><td>Check installation status and port availability, then exit</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--working-dir DIR</span></td><td>Phoenix DB directory (default: Phoenix-determined, usually <code>~/.phoenix</code>)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--sync-datasets GLOB</span></td><td>Upload golden-set JSON files matching the glob to Phoenix Datasets</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--reset / --yes</span></td><td>Delete all traces/projects/datasets from the Phoenix DB (stop Phoenix first) / skip the confirmation prompt</td></tr>
      </tbody></table>
<pre>agent-eval monitor
agent-eval monitor --sync-datasets 'data/golden_datasets/*.json'</pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cls-card" id="cli-opencode" style="margin-top:12px">
    <div class="cls-head"><span class="cls-name">agent-eval opencode</span> / <span class="cls-name">agent-eval claude</span><span class="kind fn">CLI</span><span class="cls-src">cli/opencode.py · cli/claude.py</span></div>
    <div class="cls-body">
      <div class="cls-desc">Install / manage the LiveGuardrail integration for OpenCode (a thin Node/Bun stdio-client plugin) or Claude Code (PreToolUse/PostToolUse/SessionEnd hooks). Gate B/E judgment logic always stays in Python <code>LiveGuardrail</code>; the plugin/hook is just the bridge. Both tools expose the same four subcommands.</div>
      <table class="mtable"><thead><tr><th>Subcommand</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td><span class="p">install</span></td><td>Copy the plugin/hook into the location the tool auto-loads from</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">upgrade</span></td><td>Re-copy the plugin <code>.ts</code> / refresh hooks after a package update, keeping your <code>*.config.json</code> edits (deep-merges only new keys)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">doctor</span></td><td>Verify the install: plugin/hook freshness + a live Python stdio round-trip (<code>--json</code> / <code>--no-live</code> / <code>--strict</code>)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">uninstall</span></td><td>Remove the plugin/hook + MCP entries + session state. Run <strong>before</strong> <code>pip uninstall</code> (<code>--purge</code> / <code>--dry-run</code> / <code>--yes</code>)</td></tr>
      </tbody></table>
      <table class="mtable" style="margin-top:8px"><thead><tr><th>install Option</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--global</span></td><td>Install for all projects (<code>~/.config/opencode/plugin/</code> or <code>~/.claude/</code>) instead of project-local (default)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--force</span></td><td>Overwrite an existing installed plugin/hook file</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--with-violation-search</span></td><td>Also register the <code>search_violations</code> stdio MCP server (requires <code>pip install "agent-evaluator[mcp]"</code>)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--with-recommend-fix</span></td><td>Also register the <code>recommend_fix</code> MCP server — static Gate/metric remediation lookup, no result file needed</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--with-ask-insights</span></td><td>Also register the <code>ask_insights</code> MCP server — query a result JSON's insight layer</td></tr>
      </tbody></table>
<pre>agent-eval claude install --with-violation-search --with-ask-insights
agent-eval opencode doctor --strict</pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cls-card" id="cli-loop" style="margin-top:12px">
    <div class="cls-head"><span class="cls-name">agent-eval target · benchmark · experiment · improve</span><span class="kind fn">CLI</span><span class="cls-src">cli/targets.py · benchmark.py · experiment.py · improve.py</span></div>
    <div class="cls-body">
      <div class="cls-desc">The SLO / reference-frame / closed-improvement-loop commands. State lives under <code>.aoo/</code> (<code>targets.json</code>, <code>reference.json</code>, <code>experiments.jsonl</code>, <code>improve/</code>, <code>recommendation_outcomes.jsonl</code>).</div>
      <table class="mtable"><thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td><span class="p">target set / show</span></td><td>Pin project SLOs (<code>--gate A=0.85 --tcr 90</code>) to <code>.aoo/targets.json</code>. Once set, <code>agent-eval gate</code> auto-loads them and every "below target" line in the report/insights measures against your bar, not <code>0.7</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">benchmark set / show</span></td><td>Pin an external reference distribution (<code>--tcr 78 --gate A=0.75</code>, or <code>--from-results results/</code>) to <code>.aoo/reference.json</code>. <code>insights.reference_frame</code> then reports the run's percentile + gap to the frontier</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">experiment register / list / score</span></td><td>Register a hypothesis (<code>--gate A --field avg_subtask_completion --predict-delta 0.08</code>), then <code>score v3.json --baseline v2.json --persist</code> to write verdicts back</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">improve plan / start / verify / patch</span></td><td>Closed loop: per-gate proposals → register each as an experiment + write stubs → score predicted-vs-actual and resolve → emit a unified diff per proposal (never auto-applies)</td></tr>
      </tbody></table>
<pre>agent-eval target set --gate A=0.85 --gate E=0.95 --tcr 90
agent-eval improve plan v3.json --baseline v2.json</pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cls-card" id="cli-trend" style="margin-top:12px">
    <div class="cls-head"><span class="cls-name">agent-eval trend</span><span class="kind fn">CLI</span><span class="cls-src">cli/trend.py</span></div>
    <div class="cls-body">
      <div class="cls-desc">Reads JSON result files in a directory chronologically and computes a linear slope per metric (TCR, accuracy, P95 latency, hallucination rate) to detect sustained decline. Positional <code>results_dir</code>. Exit <code>1</code> on regression when <code>--fail-on-regression</code> is set, otherwise always <code>0</code>.</div>
      <table class="mtable"><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--window N / -w</span></td><td>Number of most recent files to analyze (default: 10)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--pattern GLOB</span></td><td>Filename glob pattern (default: <code>'*.json'</code>)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--slope-threshold FLOAT</span></td><td>Slopes below this absolute value are classified "stable" (default: 0.3). Unit: %/run for TCR·accuracy·hallucination, s/run for latency</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--fail-on-regression</span></td><td>Exit code <code>1</code> on regression (CI/CD failure)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="p">--output-json PATH</span></td><td>Save analysis results to a JSON file</td></tr>
      </tbody></table>
<pre>agent-eval trend results/ --window 20 --fail-on-regression</pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

