<!-- ── LiveGuardrail ── -->
<section class="sec" id="live-guardrail">
  <div class="sec-title">🛡️ LiveGuardrail <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:400;color:var(--text2);margin-left:8px">Real-Time Guardrail</span></div>
  <div class="sec-sub">Every Gate above scores a session <em>after</em> it finishes. <code>LiveGuardrail</code> checks a single tool call <em>before</em> it executes and can block it — reusing the exact same Gate B (Behavioral Integrity) and Gate E (Security Boundary) evaluators that power batch scoring, just invoked synchronously per tool call instead of per session. No new detection logic.</div>

  <div class="cls-card">
    <div class="cls-head"><span class="cls-name">LiveVerdict</span><span class="kind cls">dataclass</span><span class="cls-src">agent_evaluator.gates.live_guardrail</span></div>
    <div class="cls-body">
      <div class="cls-desc">Return value of <code>check_before_tool_call()</code>.</div>
      <table class="mtable">
        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><span class="p">block</span></td><td><span class="t">bool</span></td><td><code>True</code> means this tool call should be blocked</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">gate</span></td><td><span class="t">Optional[str]</span></td><td><code>"B"</code> | <code>"E"</code> | <code>None</code> — which Gate triggered the block</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">reason</span></td><td><span class="t">Optional[str]</span></td><td>Human-readable reason (empty when <code>block=False</code>)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">detail</span></td><td><span class="t">Dict[str, Any]</span></td><td>Full result from the underlying evaluator/tracker (empty dict when <code>block=False</code>)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cls-card" style="margin-top:12px">
    <div class="cls-head"><span class="cls-name">LiveGuardrail</span><span class="kind cls">class</span><span class="cls-src">agent_evaluator.gates.live_guardrail</span></div>
    <div class="cls-body">
      <div class="cls-desc">One instance per session (agent loop run) — internal state (<code>_tool_calls</code>) is not lock-protected, so sharing one instance across concurrent sessions is unsafe. All constructor parameters are optional; only pass the Gate B Configs / Gate E trackers you want active. Every internal exception <strong>fails open</strong> (never blocks a call because of a guardrail bug).</div>
      <div class="slbl">Constructor Parameters — detectors</div>
      {% call param_table() %}
          <tr><td><span class="p">loop_detection</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">LoopDetectionConfig</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Gate B — same config class as <code>@agent_eval(loop_detection=...)</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">deadlock</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">DeadlockConfig</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Gate B — circular delegation detection</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">scope</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">ScopeConfig</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Gate B — allowed/forbidden tool lists (matching is case-insensitive)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">tool_parameter_safety</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">ToolParameterSafetyConfig</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Gate B — dangerous argument pattern matching (also decodes base64/hex payloads)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">tool_authorization</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">ToolAuthorizationTracker</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Gate E — pass a tracker <em>instance</em>, not a Config (this one is stateful). Has a non-customizable hard-coded backstop (<code>rm -rf</code>, <code>sudo</code>, <code>eval(</code>, <code>DROP TABLE</code> …) that scans every argument</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">privilege_escalation</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">PrivilegeEscalationDetector</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Gate E — pass a tracker instance</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">tool_chain_attack</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">ToolChainAttackDetector</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Gate E — pass a tracker instance</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">team_concurrency</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">TeamConcurrencyConfig</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Block a write into a path another developer has an active <code>.aoo/claims.jsonl</code> scope claim on. Claims + shared-file list are read <strong>once</strong> at construction (call <code>refresh_team_claims()</code> to reload)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">branch_guard</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">BranchGuardConfig</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Block a direct <code>git commit</code>/<code>git push</code> on a protected branch (default <code>main</code>/<code>master</code>). Re-checks the current branch just before a git mutation unless <code>recheck_branch=False</code></td></tr>
      {% endcall %}
      <div class="slbl">Constructor Parameters — real-time tuning knobs</div>
      <div class="cls-desc" style="margin-bottom:6px">These affect only the live <code>check_before_tool_call()</code> path — the batch <code>snapshot()</code> still sees full history and full scans, so a live "allow" and the final report stay consistent.</div>
      {% call param_table() %}
          <tr><td><span class="p">live_loop_window</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">int | None</span></td><td><code>15</code></td><td>Trailing window of recent calls the live loop check looks at. Prevents one early repeat from latching the guardrail closed for the rest of the session. <code>None</code> = whole session (old behavior)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">live_loop_blocking_types</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">tuple[str, ...]</span></td><td><code>("consecutive_repeat",)</code></td><td>Which loop types actually <em>block</em> when <code>on_loop_detected="fail"</code>. <code>"window_duplicate"</code> / <code>"response_similarity"</code> are recorded to <code>snapshot()</code> only unless added here</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">lenient_shell_file_write</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">bool</span></td><td><code>True</code></td><td>A pure file write via shell (<code>cat/tee/echo/printf</code> redirect or heredoc, no <code>;</code> <code>&amp;&amp;</code> <code>|</code> <code>$(…)</code> backticks) is treated like <code>Write</code>/<code>Edit</code> — dangerous strings in the file <em>content</em> don't block. Set <code>False</code> to scan heredoc bodies too</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">protected_write_paths</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">tuple[str, ...] | None</span></td><td><em>ssh/aws/gnupg keys · shell rc · cron · /etc · systemd …</em></td><td>Regex list — a write whose <em>target path</em> matches is blocked (Gate E) regardless of content. <code>None</code>/<code>()</code> disables the check</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">auth_scan_skip_keys</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">tuple[str, ...]</span></td><td><em>content · old_string/new_string · patch · diff · todos …</em></td><td>Parameter keys carrying <em>file content / patch text</em> are excluded from the hard-coded auth backstop scan, so writing a README that documents <code>sudo apt install</code> isn't blocked. <code>()</code> restores the old full scan</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">max_tool_output_chars</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">int</span></td><td><code>2000</code></td><td>Truncation length for <code>record_tool_call(output={"stdout": …, "stderr": …})</code></td></tr>
      {% endcall %}
      <div class="slbl">Key Methods</div>
      <table class="mtable">
        <thead><tr><th>Method Signature</th><th>Return</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><span class="p">check_before_tool_call(task_id, tool_name, parameters=None)</span></td><td><span class="r">LiveVerdict</span></td><td>Pure query — does <strong>not</strong> mutate internal state, and never records a blocked attempt. Evaluates the candidate call against existing history plus this one call.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">record_tool_call(task_id, tool_name, parameters=None, output=None)</span></td><td><span class="r">None</span></td><td>Confirms a call that actually executed. Call only after a <code>block=False</code> verdict. <code>output</code> is a dict with any of <code>success</code> (bool) · <code>exit_code</code> (int) · <code>stdout</code> · <code>stderr</code> — <code>success</code> feeds Gate G's tool success rate.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">record_blocked_attempt(task_id, tool_name, verdict)</span></td><td><span class="r">None</span></td><td>Opt-in audit log of a fully-blocked attempt, kept separate from the Gate B/E scoring history. <code>verdict</code> must have <code>block=True</code> (raises <code>ValueError</code> otherwise).</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">refresh_team_claims()</span></td><td><span class="r">None</span></td><td>Reload the <code>team_concurrency</code> claims + shared-file cache (constructor reads them once).</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">snapshot()</span></td><td><span class="r">Dict[str, Any]</span></td><td>Gate B/E evaluation results for all confirmed calls so far, keyed the same way as <code>TaskResult.extra</code> (<code>loop_detection</code>, <code>scope</code>, <code>tool_authorization</code>, …). Side-effect free — safe to call repeatedly.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">to_task_extra()</span></td><td><span class="r">Dict[str, Any]</span></td><td>Alias of <code>snapshot()</code>, named for its intended use: assign to <code>TaskResult(extra=...)</code> to feed a session's final verdict into the normal batch report.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="note tip" style="margin-top:10px">🔑 <strong>Loop verdict keying</strong>: the live loop check keys on <em>(tool name + SHA-1 of sorted args)</em>, so a varied <code>bash</code> → <code>bash</code> → <code>bash</code> sequence with different commands is not a loop.</div>
      <div class="note tip" style="margin-top:12px">💡 <strong>Reference integration</strong>: <code>opencode-plugin/</code> (repo root) wires <code>LiveGuardrail</code> into <a href="https://opencode.ai" target="_blank">OpenCode</a>'s <code>tool.execute.before</code>/<code>after</code> hooks via a Python subprocess bridge (<code>agent_evaluator.integrations.live_guardrail_stdio</code> / <code>live_guardrail_report</code>) — live-tested against a real local Ollama session, but shipped as a prototype reference, not part of the pip package. Install it with <code>agent-eval opencode install</code> (or <code>agent-eval claude install</code> for the Claude Code hook).</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cls-card" style="margin-top:12px" id="tool-guard">
    <div class="cls-head"><span class="cls-name">@tool_guard</span> · <span class="cls-name">live_guardrail_session()</span><span class="kind fn">decorator + context manager</span><span class="cls-src">agent_evaluator.gates.live_guardrail</span></div>
    <div class="cls-body">
      <div class="cls-desc">Non-invasive wrapper so you don't hand-write <code>check_before_tool_call()</code> / <code>record_tool_call()</code> at every call site. Decorate each tool function with <code>@tool_guard</code>, then run the agent loop inside a <code>live_guardrail_session()</code> block — the decorated calls are checked before and recorded after automatically. Works on sync and <code>async def</code> tools. No new detection logic; a pure application layer over <code>LiveGuardrail</code>.</div>
      <div class="slbl"><code>tool_guard(tool_name=None, *, audit_blocked=False, fail_closed=False, capture_output=None)</code></div>
      {% call param_table() %}
          <tr><td><span class="p">tool_name</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">str | None</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Name passed to the guardrail. Defaults to the wrapped function's <code>__name__</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">audit_blocked</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">bool</span></td><td><code>False</code></td><td>Also call <code>record_blocked_attempt()</code> when a call is blocked</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">fail_closed</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">bool</span></td><td><code>False</code></td><td>If no <code>live_guardrail_session()</code> is active: <code>True</code> raises <code>RuntimeError</code>; <code>False</code> emits a <code>RuntimeWarning</code> and runs the tool unguarded (kept fail-open for tests/REPLs — set <code>True</code> in production)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">capture_output</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">Callable[[Any], dict]</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Maps the tool's return value to <code>{"success":…, "exit_code":…, "stdout":…, "stderr":…}</code> for <code>record_tool_call(output=…)</code>. Omitted → no output inferred. A raised exception is always recorded as <code>success=False</code></td></tr>
      {% endcall %}
      <table class="mtable">
        <thead><tr><th>Symbol</th><th>Kind</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><span class="p">live_guardrail_session(guardrail, task_id)</span></td><td><span class="r">context manager</span></td><td>Binds the guardrail + task_id (via <code>contextvars</code>, so concurrent <code>asyncio</code> tasks stay isolated) for every <code>@tool_guard</code> call inside the <code>with</code> block. Enter once per session.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">GuardrailBlockedError</span></td><td><span class="r">exception</span></td><td>Raised out of a <code>@tool_guard</code> call when blocked. <code>.verdict</code> holds the <code>LiveVerdict</code> (<code>.gate</code> / <code>.reason</code> / <code>.detail</code>).</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
<pre style="margin-top:10px"><span class="kw">from</span> <span class="cn">agent_evaluator.gates.live_guardrail</span> <span class="kw">import</span> (
    LiveGuardrail, tool_guard, live_guardrail_session, GuardrailBlockedError,
)
<span class="kw">from</span> <span class="cn">agent_evaluator.gates.gate_b_behavioral.configs</span> <span class="kw">import</span> LoopDetectionConfig, ToolParameterSafetyConfig

guardrail = <span class="fn">LiveGuardrail</span>(
    loop_detection=<span class="fn">LoopDetectionConfig</span>(consecutive_repeat_threshold=<span class="nm">6</span>),
    tool_parameter_safety=<span class="fn">ToolParameterSafetyConfig</span>(fail_on_dangerous=<span class="kw">True</span>),
)

<span class="de">@tool_guard</span>(audit_blocked=<span class="kw">True</span>, fail_closed=<span class="kw">True</span>)
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">bash</span>(command: str) -&gt; str:
    <span class="kw">return</span> subprocess.<span class="fn">run</span>(command, shell=<span class="kw">True</span>, capture_output=<span class="kw">True</span>, text=<span class="kw">True</span>).stdout

<span class="kw">with</span> <span class="fn">live_guardrail_session</span>(guardrail, task_id=<span class="st">"session-1"</span>):
    <span class="kw">try</span>:
        <span class="fn">bash</span>(<span class="st">"ls -la"</span>)                 <span class="cm"># checked → runs → recorded</span>
        <span class="fn">bash</span>(<span class="st">"rm -rf /"</span>)               <span class="cm"># blocked</span>
    <span class="kw">except</span> GuardrailBlockedError <span class="kw">as</span> e:
        <span class="fn">print</span>(f<span class="st">"blocked by Gate {e.verdict.gate}: {e.verdict.reason}"</span>)

<span class="cm"># feed the session's Gate B/E verdict into the batch report</span>
monitor.<span class="fn">record_task</span>(<span class="fn">create_taskresult</span>(<span class="st">"session-1"</span>, <span class="st">"..."</span>, <span class="st">"..."</span>, extra=guardrail.<span class="fn">to_task_extra</span>()))</pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cls-card" style="margin-top:12px" id="guardrail-configs">
    <div class="cls-head"><span class="cls-name">TeamConcurrencyConfig</span> · <span class="cls-name">BranchGuardConfig</span><span class="kind cls">dataclass</span><span class="cls-src">agent_evaluator.gates.team_concurrency / .branch_guard</span></div>
    <div class="cls-body">
      <div class="cls-desc"><code>TeamConcurrencyConfig</code> — pair with <code>agent-eval claims</code>. When another developer holds an active scope claim on a path, a write there is blocked (Gate E). <code>owner="auto"</code> resolves to <code>git config user.name</code> and excludes your own claims.</div>
      {% call field_table() %}
          <tr><td><span class="p">claims_path</span></td><td><span class="t">str</span></td><td><code>".aoo/claims.jsonl"</code> — scope-claim log</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">shared_files_path</span></td><td><span class="t">str | None</span></td><td><code>None</code> — file whose lines list paths that always need coordination, claim or not</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">scoped_tool_names</span></td><td><span class="t">tuple[str, ...]</span></td><td>Write-type tool names this check applies to</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">path_param_candidates</span></td><td><span class="t">tuple[str, ...]</span></td><td>Parameter keys inspected for the target path</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">owner</span></td><td><span class="t">str | None</span></td><td><code>None</code> — this session's developer; <code>"auto"</code> → <code>git config user.name</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">fail_on_conflict</span></td><td><span class="t">bool</span></td><td><code>True</code> — block (vs. record-only) on an overlapping claim</td></tr>
      {% endcall %}
      <div class="cls-desc" style="margin-top:10px"><code>BranchGuardConfig</code> — block a direct commit/push on a protected branch before it happens (fail-open).</div>
      {% call field_table() %}
          <tr><td><span class="p">protected_branches</span></td><td><span class="t">tuple[str, ...]</span></td><td><code>("main", "master")</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">git_mutation_patterns</span></td><td><span class="t">tuple[str, ...]</span></td><td><code>(r"git\s+commit", r"git\s+push")</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">require_branch_prefix</span></td><td><span class="t">str | None</span></td><td><code>None</code> — also require the working branch to start with this prefix</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">scoped_tool_names</span></td><td><span class="t">tuple[str, ...]</span></td><td><code>("bash", "Bash")</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">fail_on_violation</span></td><td><span class="t">bool</span></td><td><code>True</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">recheck_branch</span></td><td><span class="t">bool</span></td><td><code>True</code> — re-read the current branch just before a git mutation (catches <code>git checkout main</code> mid-session)</td></tr>
      {% endcall %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── 프레임워크 통합 ── -->
<section class="sec" id="frameworks">
  <div class="sec-title">🔗 24 Framework Adapters</div>
  <div class="sec-sub">Connect with a single <code>@agent_eval(monitor, framework="...")</code> line. The adapter automatically extracts <strong>tokens_used · tool_calls · chain_steps · agent_interactions</strong> from the response object and populates TaskResult.</div>

  <!-- 패턴 설명 -->
  <div class="cls-card">
    <div class="cls-head"><span class="cls-name">Common Pattern</span><span class="kind fn">decorator</span></div>
    <div class="cls-body">
<pre><span class="kw">from</span> <span class="cn">agent_evaluator</span> <span class="kw">import</span> PerformanceMonitor
<span class="kw">from</span> <span class="cn">agent_evaluator.decorators</span> <span class="kw">import</span> agent_eval

monitor = <span class="fn">PerformanceMonitor</span>(output_dir=<span class="st">"results/"</span>)

<span class="cm"># Same pattern for all 24 frameworks — just change the framework= parameter</span>
<span class="de">@agent_eval</span>(monitor, task_type=<span class="st">"qa"</span>, framework=<span class="st">"openai"</span>)
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">my_agent</span>(question: str, ground_truth: str = <span class="st">""</span>) -> str:
    <span class="kw">return</span> client.chat.completions.<span class="fn">create</span>(...)  <span class="cm"># Return the response object as-is</span>

<span class="cm"># Omit framework= for auto-detection via response attributes (auto_detect_framework=True by default)</span>
<span class="de">@agent_eval</span>(monitor, task_type=<span class="st">"qa"</span>)           <span class="cm"># Auto-detects 12 types including anthropic/openai/gemini etc.</span>
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">auto_agent</span>(question: str, ground_truth: str = <span class="st">""</span>) -> str: ...</pre>
    </div>
  </div>

